1. What is Linux Architecture?

Linux Architecture describes how different components of the Linux operating system work together.

Think of Linux as a building with multiple floors.

Each floor has a different responsibility.

Users interact with applications, applications interact with the kernel, and the kernel communicates with the hardware.

